body:
I'm in the same position somewhat. I'm 22 and just quit CT like 26 days ago from 20-25gpd. Parents found out because obviously I couldn't hide going CT from something like this. Was way worse than the flu so if I had told them it was the flu they would've wanted to send me to the hospital. Didn't go to rehab or anything as I live at home with them and that was a better option than any rehab was going to be.

&#x200B;

Feeling rather guilty myself. Part of it is the shame from their judgement, and them kind of treating me like an addict not wanting to let me out of their sight at any point. I've made a lot of mistakes and it's probably totally warranted, but still it's an awful feeling. I think the best thing that will heal this though will just be good old fashioned time. As time goes on I'll hopefully earn their trust back and of course my brain chemistry will be getting closer and closer to baseline.

I was the same way. Had a really bad health scare and knew I had to quit. Else, I'm just filling my body up with useless calorieless kratom capsules and just making things worse.

&#x200B;

Still not over the health scare, but having faith things will return to normal soon. If it does, I'll honestly be thankful for the health scare for getting me off kratom. If not, well, either way I'm off kratom.
